erif';"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_OLdAZQF0f0-1NJLulxlneg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SalesTypeAndDirectFinancingLeasesLeaseReceivablePaymentsToBeReceived" scale="3" id="Tc_Ne_hnTS1fEO5zRILLMSVQw_4_3">298</ix:nonFraction></span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.01%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">As of June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and December 31, 2025 the carrying amount of the lease receivables was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_OLdAZQF0f0-1NJLulxlneg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SalesTypeLeaseLeaseReceivable" scale="6" id="Narr_qBo_q29eVEWb40bd7rOZVA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_FY6ZAtOH2UObH0ihkkk-OQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SalesTypeLeaseLeaseReceivable" scale="6" id="Narr_ruuxEWzi_UOIrP3ADse7Ow">0.3</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million, for both periods. The Company does <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_OLdAZQF0f0-1NJLulxlneg" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:SalesTypeLeaseUnguaranteedResidualAsset" scale="3" id="Narr_UMC5QSQtZEGIhJ3HJ631tA">no</ix:nonFraction>t have any unguaranteed residual assets.</p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Lessor operating leases:</p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">The Systems leased to customers subsequent to January 1, 2019 for which collection is not probable are accounted for as operating leases. For the three months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025, the Company recognized operating lease income of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_2Znuu00P8UyS9hLoxwyGpg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLeaseIncome" scale="6" id="Narr_OL_DJeL9wk2PxRB2d8xTGw">0.06</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_CXeMpMWZWE-nV-SD8OWUtw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLeaseIncome" scale="6" id="Narr_M97dM_5YKESVJDtOsuXBgg">0.05</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively. For the six months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025, the Company recognized operating lease income of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_NrFZM9V-EU2Sxr_n17urxw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLeaseIncome" scale="6" id="Narr_5uwit14EGkiwUA7WqDHwYA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026__wQNUBlkhUu7xmPgn_toEg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLeaseIncome" scale="6" id="Narr_FJlS_5ANwkaSUTojXbx-sA">0.1</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million, for both periods. </p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">The Company maintained rental equipment, net, of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_PropertyPlantAndEquipmentByTypeAxis_us-gaap_MachineryAndEquipmentMember_s6Brw2B_jkq0R3zOQaJf6w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PropertyPlantAndEquipmentNet" scale="6" id="Narr_lrSXXv3DTUquoj9gwG0CPw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_PropertyPlantAndEquipmentByTypeAxis_us-gaap_MachineryAndEquipmentMember_sFuY74gQU0qDkzb5yqg63g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PropertyPlantAndEquipmentNet" scale="6" id="Narr_p-xzW_4kG0SEQ3bdfmle3Q">0.1</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million for both June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and December&#160;31,&#160;2025, which are included in property and equipment, net on the consolidated balance sheets. Rental equipment depreciation expense was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_PropertyPlantAndEquipmentByTypeAxis_us-gaap_MachineryAndEquipmentMember_9-Hp3vOYoE-MiXOzxUfLVA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" id="Narr_P1QpF8UlF0mMBj0bjhATQg">0.01</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_PropertyPlantAndEquipmentByTypeAxis_us-gaap_MachineryAndEquipmentMember_x09qbNxFN0O9eDyobHr5CA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" id="Narr_v7k60qrkwUCuYQpeqPGHbA">0.14</ix:nonFraction> million for the three months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025, respectively and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_PropertyPlantAndEquipmentByTypeAxis_us-gaap_MachineryAndEquipmentMember_5UMVU7rOKUuFeHmElnk9sQ" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" id="Narr_1iLz9dWn40GU0_xIkEwRKw">0.03</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_PropertyPlantAndEquipmentByTypeAxis_us-gaap_MachineryAndEquipmentMember_jnUgn1YWLEafwAR5KSReLg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" id="Narr_XQVxCDV0U0Gp1QqxtobeNA">0.16</ix:nonFraction> million for the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively. </p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026__wQNUBlkhUu7xmPgn_toEg" name="us-gaap:DeferredCostsCapitalizedPrepaidAndOtherAssetsDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_kcgjR1G0QkuSNbSfjWVsMg" continuedAt="Tb_kcgjR1G0QkuSNbSfjWVsMg_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">11.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;PREPAID COMMISSION EXPENSE</p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">The Company pays a commission on both System sales and treatment session sales. Since the commission paid for the System sales is not commensurate with the commission paid for treatment sessions, the Company capitalizes commission expense associated with the System commissions paid that is incremental to specifically anticipated future treatment session orders. In developing this estimate, the Company </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">15</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;"><a style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';" href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:9pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NEURONETICS,&#160;INC.</p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes&#160;to Interim Consolidated Financial Statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(Unaudited)</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_kcgjR1G0QkuSNbSfjWVsMg_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">considered its historical treatment session sales and customer retention rates, as well as technology development life cycles and other industry factors. These costs are periodically reviewed for impairment.</p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">The System commissions are deferred and amortized on a straight-line basis over a <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026__wQNUBlkhUu7xmPgn_toEg" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="stim:AmortizationPeriodOfDeferredSalesCommissions" id="Narr_hMsVlh2CHUCP7nNJaIFMFw">seven year</ix:nonNumeric> period equal to the average customer term, which the Company deems to be the expected period of benefit for these costs.</p><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">On the Company&#8217;s consolidated balance sheets, the current portion of capitalized contract costs is presented in current portion of prepaid commission expense, while the long-term portion is included in prepaid commission expense. Amortization expense was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_CXeMpMWZWE-nV-SD8OWUtw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDeferredSalesCommissions" scale="6" id="Narr_TEoJOtdUFk-akaxM1WD6tg"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_2Znuu00P8UyS9hLoxwyGpg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDeferredSalesCommissions" scale="6" id="Narr_3hhU5RodSkOpEQoLs9q-sA">0.8</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million for both of the three months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025 and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_NrFZM9V-EU2Sxr_n17urxw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDeferredSalesCommissions" scale="6" id="Narr_Vs7Y9xpIsEenBlVgpq63QQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bBHOybMHY0qDJ0mcCjRxyQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026__wQNUBlkhUu7xmPgn_toEg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDeferredSalesCommissions" scale="6" id="Narr_DNEScRZ2bkGv2ycK0EsZqg">1.6</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million for both of the six months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025. </p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;margin-bottom:10pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><a id="_c67efad9_b4b3_4eb5_bf4e_304674e20f64"></a><a id="Tc_mQjuHPbj-kO-MMCE-Es_gQ_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_RPkMocrCSkGDqt_Vb4A1KA_1_5"></a><a id="Tc_12X9drbk7EK2e36frXqpJg_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_jfPoLkQt-ECgdChFwTydhQ_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_QrHo9d8mDUSpvSLWE2VH6A_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_rl8fgRZe70GbEOTTGgXY1A_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_pPb3tV1asEKalupH3jgQ6Q_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_J5R0-ypP40uWPkiqn9gEQg_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_hgDTKkXRGUiXNKmrJFtCxg_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_ucTiF3iMuUGZe4oFhO1iOg_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_hpGlfiTP10CfAMNeCxzPLg_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_nA89iyVr5UeeknNQUgZ-aw_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_elKo4wymEkOt_s2Rd0OTNw_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_aFXIjw59CUOoHuQUEd50WQ_10_0"></a><a id="Tc_E1MmZjoO3UuRC1Gq3ArNPQ_10_2"></a><a id="Tc_p9ZpT2ozi0CALIhm8Uu38w_10_5"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026__wQNUBlkhUu7xmPgn_toEg" name="us-gaap:AccountsPayableAndAccruedLiabilitiesDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_WpxODnLlcUuTd1R9UjIJKw" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">12.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;ACCRUED EXPENSES</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026__wQNUBlkhUu7xmPgn_toEg" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfAccruedLiabilitiesTableTextBlock" id="Tb_LFwmrF2tXkKTsGteLj2Yrg" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">The following table presents the composition of accrued expenses as of June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and December&#160;31,&#160;2025 (in thousands):</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:70.01%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.54%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height